  "vendor_website": "sensym.com.br",
  "description": "PID process controller with ramp and soak (96 x 48): 8 programs of 8 points, one control output and up to three alarms, thermocouple, Pt-100, Ni-120, voltage and current inputs, with RS-485 Modbus",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-11-13",
  "source": "Sensym, TCY-46R Manual de instalacao e operacao V1.0 (section 6, Modbus address table)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "TCY-46R Controlador de Processo PID com Rampa e Patamar 96 x 48, Manual de instalacao e operacao",
      "version": "1.0",
      "url": "https://sensym.com.br/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Manual-TCY-46R.pdf",
      "note": "section 6 and the parameter descriptions, linked in issue #394"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The addresses are written in hexadecimal in the document and are taken as the addresses sent on the wire (address_base 0): the process value is 0x1000 (4096), the control setpoint 0x1. The document does not say which function reads or writes them; they are taken as holding registers (FC03, FC06).",
    "The document does not give the scaling. Values are taken as integers whose decimal point is set by the decimal point parameter (0x23); the document says the value limits follow the ranges it gives for each parameter in the programming section.",
    "Serial settings are selectable in the instrument: 2400, 4800, 9600, 19200 or 38400 bps, ASCII or RTU, 7 or 8 data bits, even, none or odd parity, 1 or 2 stop bits. From the factory it is ASCII, 7 bits, even parity, 1 stop bit and 2400 bps: to use RTU change the communication mode and the message length to 8 bits (the values here are for that setup). The slave address default is not given; 1 is a placeholder. The device can also be set as a master.",
    "Not every parameter is present on every version: alarms 2 and 3, the analog retransmission output and the analog control output depend on the model ordered.",
    "The calibration registers for the retransmission output are printed in the document as 3EH, 40H and 3FH (offset, zero, span), so the span is at 3FH and the zero at 40H. The registers are listed as printed.",
    "The TCY-46R and the TCY-48R share the same address table; only the case size differs.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baudrate": 2400,
  "parity": "E",
  "databits": 8,
  "stopbits": 1,
  "address_base": 0,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "x_status": "official",
